cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kaan (कान): Acoustic Grain Pest Detector for Indian Farmers"
message: "If you use Project Kaan, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dhiman
    given-names: Arnav
    email: arnavd371@gmail.com
    website: "https://arnavdportfolio.vercel.app/"
    alias: arnavd371
repository-code: "https://github.com/arnavd371/Project-Kaan"
url: "https://kaan-web.vercel.app"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-04"
abstract: >-
  Kaan listens to stored grain using a smartphone microphone, converts audio to
  a mel spectrogram, and classifies clean grain versus rice weevil, lesser grain
  borer, or red flour beetle with an on-device INT8 CNN. Version 3 ships a
  production model distilled from classical + deep teachers; version 2 added a
  leakage-aware multi-approach bake-off.
keywords:
  - acoustic pest detection
  - stored grain
  - agriculture
  - tensorflow lite
  - onnx
  - india
  - open source
